[{:db/id "q-35689/selection/e2feda7f09f869f311a30c1bf4c822e182d07eb2815ece87a2b1855237a0e023" :answer/id #uuid "1216c78b-ab54-5b03-a07f-676894944c33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35689/selection/6d6dd5d363d45802f93bab0fb8393e5ccab35fdb36e2b490c0f9ce25506397df" :answer/id #uuid "2b5dc9ea-bafd-54dc-bdc2-68a8171405b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35689/selection/cc1adae20825e521c1f573a603621fa113a51e658393fe500daad594ba7629a8" :answer/id #uuid "7a4974c8-d520-508d-ae18-8ef5622aab4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35689/selection/91876273f4710faf58b3c25364cfb4326bfb684696ec1e2f53b48dcaebb3967f" :answer/id #uuid "30a9b801-aeb8-5ab8-a393-2cde0442b1b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35689/selection/41f664b045b7ae8bb6474a311802c5185f0b674ea18bcdd7c4469609388f0860" :answer/id #uuid "ed058997-8ad5-54c2-8557-0e8e16b8f9ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35689/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c0766a9-a4b4-5927-8a5a-32dc01fe7659" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-35689/selection/6d6dd5d363d45802f93bab0fb8393e5ccab35fdb36e2b490c0f9ce25506397df" :answer-field/choices ["q-35689/selection/e2feda7f09f869f311a30c1bf4c822e182d07eb2815ece87a2b1855237a0e023" "q-35689/selection/6d6dd5d363d45802f93bab0fb8393e5ccab35fdb36e2b490c0f9ce25506397df" "q-35689/selection/cc1adae20825e521c1f573a603621fa113a51e658393fe500daad594ba7629a8" "q-35689/selection/91876273f4710faf58b3c25364cfb4326bfb684696ec1e2f53b48dcaebb3967f" "q-35689/selection/41f664b045b7ae8bb6474a311802c5185f0b674ea18bcdd7c4469609388f0860"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-35689" :question/id #uuid "8f8f7997-5431-5c08-819e-4fce158922f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-35689" :question/problem "Let $B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}$ and $C={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}$ be bases of ${R}^{2}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $C$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ relative to the basis $B.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-35689/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f989cbaf-2d99-5267-8864-48a48db2d535"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-35689"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81847/selection/d9a2102f00aea20c41b3423f453528b49d1fa2365181a3c904e64d90e3349fc6" :answer/id #uuid "36fd555b-2b28-5474-8d65-ea0936e4d935" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81847/selection/18096e3f0b415fbf35470a6c1b0519f1af234607488ab8a6be74646cc84e2fc7" :answer/id #uuid "f24d9346-27c8-5644-9a0a-f274f5c3c214" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81847/selection/b6b5ce5238ac0326a5a5f8912c2772859a6609e0d5ea0ad6626fa4d1c474bf94" :answer/id #uuid "09e0741e-a563-5229-85c7-c3c06e32b79c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 11 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81847/selection/de3da114cbc44efedba648373376709b8132672158c3077888f5f5f240a8510f" :answer/id #uuid "6631ad0d-0998-5dd9-a2d5-a99bcab64b27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81847/selection/f675ab811eb2cc7ed7875454f58a71e7d696c3e6a2f6e4bd9fe480ed27f50353" :answer/id #uuid "d174798c-8d6e-567f-bd6d-4919452d844e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 11 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81847/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e39f4256-42ce-57b6-94f7-20b3ce428065" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81847/selection/d9a2102f00aea20c41b3423f453528b49d1fa2365181a3c904e64d90e3349fc6" :answer-field/choices ["q-81847/selection/d9a2102f00aea20c41b3423f453528b49d1fa2365181a3c904e64d90e3349fc6" "q-81847/selection/18096e3f0b415fbf35470a6c1b0519f1af234607488ab8a6be74646cc84e2fc7" "q-81847/selection/b6b5ce5238ac0326a5a5f8912c2772859a6609e0d5ea0ad6626fa4d1c474bf94" "q-81847/selection/de3da114cbc44efedba648373376709b8132672158c3077888f5f5f240a8510f" "q-81847/selection/f675ab811eb2cc7ed7875454f58a71e7d696c3e6a2f6e4bd9fe480ed27f50353"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81847" :question/id #uuid "62dadad6-bc72-59c3-b335-faab5922669e" :question/math-academy-id "q-81847" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors of $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 11\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81847/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b973d79-8fe4-5033-8202-9693004855dc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81847"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81855/selection/6a2f393c4168f0314cc98f4a446fb09fbfbe49120d425cae1483ebe174e56b17" :answer/id #uuid "0c27da77-eda0-5edc-a157-ef5b5c0ba20d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -3 \\\\ -7 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81855/selection/75d6c80a48f4ef89bc81b1f6be8c51cec93dad1e7af49201f18cd1d35912e4b4" :answer/id #uuid "e1e33884-ffab-5dd2-b550-6a7cd370dc39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81855/selection/aa712bc650660c89897d87edd06e71a5fab7b64d5bcfed1bafd33990a8adb14a" :answer/id #uuid "5db1036b-8a0c-550e-9a99-91478cedaa5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81855/selection/af7877bfd46708b0cdc31e47ae37e1d1f14ea8c5cc7a92910db64099493ae6a9" :answer/id #uuid "4821dc14-4b67-5838-9261-f50a7911fc6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81855/selection/2eb3c6a9f800d5b910295e3a944c3644c87510b13a182191ba3d93114e29ad08" :answer/id #uuid "f37e5184-51e0-5f07-a094-22228931b99c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81855/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4294d352-a4d3-5ccb-8bad-7147b8ed84fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81855/selection/af7877bfd46708b0cdc31e47ae37e1d1f14ea8c5cc7a92910db64099493ae6a9" :answer-field/choices ["q-81855/selection/6a2f393c4168f0314cc98f4a446fb09fbfbe49120d425cae1483ebe174e56b17" "q-81855/selection/75d6c80a48f4ef89bc81b1f6be8c51cec93dad1e7af49201f18cd1d35912e4b4" "q-81855/selection/aa712bc650660c89897d87edd06e71a5fab7b64d5bcfed1bafd33990a8adb14a" "q-81855/selection/af7877bfd46708b0cdc31e47ae37e1d1f14ea8c5cc7a92910db64099493ae6a9" "q-81855/selection/2eb3c6a9f800d5b910295e3a944c3644c87510b13a182191ba3d93114e29ad08"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81855" :question/id #uuid "3e562f59-572b-52a9-8296-807890374941" :question/math-academy-id "q-81855" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B$ to the basis $C$ is given by \n${P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}].$\nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$  ." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (-5)-(-7)\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81855/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23b6a85e-e1de-590c-84d2-379052b1b9f3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81855"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113105/selection/9d584e18ceb031ae693321c095dad3fb9fcf262c24183323c3ffc0bbff2870ac" :answer/id #uuid "72b1e845-1654-5ea4-8441-657059cffc72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113105/selection/34f5b43a03196ff29fbce4aeeda98a98b1cf1228acfe8517f88968dffe76b36e" :answer/id #uuid "17037c0e-e866-5a2a-b8ff-8e7743ace700" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113105/selection/3f898f18dae7626f97cbcfd49480b463374501017450f92c0b98bcf71f6881d1" :answer/id #uuid "f5d1db51-2145-58ed-85a4-173887701275" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113105/selection/ad3c294d65321de230b34c3139a8a042dbe1e9b5bfc57ae2e58d944623e7fed8" :answer/id #uuid "15afda04-9654-5db6-afb9-7f6583ac1787" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "